NVIDIA's Nemotron Parse 2.0 Turns Any Scanned Page Into Structured Data
=E2=96=B2
3,714 Likes
NVIDIA just dropped
Nemotron Parse 2.0
, a small but capable model that turns scanned pages and PDFs into clean, s=
tructured data you can actually use.
Here's the deal: you feed it a page image, it spits back text with labels, =
coordinates, and reading order. Think of it like a super-powered scanner th=
at also understands layout.
What's new in v2.0:
Charts are now supported, it can convert chart visuals into tables
Handwriting recognition improved dramatically (error rate dropped from 0.97=
 to 0.34)
Indic script accuracy jumped from 6% to 72%
Multilingual OCR score went from 44% to 91%
The model runs on a
single A100 GPU
and uses under 2GB of memory. You load it via Hugging Face Transformers, po=
int it at a PNG of your page, and get back Markdown, JSON, CSV, or HTML.
This opens up local document pipelines with no per-page API costs. Perfect =
for building search indexes, feeding RAG systems, or extracting tables into=
 databases. Weights are
commercially licensed
under OpenMDW 1.1.
