You know how AI apps need to understand text meaning, not just keywords? Th=
at's what an
embedding model
does: it converts text into numbers your app can compare. BGE Base is one o=
f the best English embedding models out there, and now it runs fully local,=
 no Python, no PyTorch.
Compendium Labs packaged it into
GGUF format
, the same format you use for local LLMs, so one runtime handles both your =
generator and your embedder. It hit 800,000 downloads.
Pick your size:
Q4_K_M at 66 MB
: small enough to bundle inside a desktop app
Q8_0 at 113 MB: better accuracy, still CPU-friendly
F16 at 209 MB: near-perfect precision for servers
Spin it up with llama.cpp or Ollama and hit a local OpenAI-compatible endpo=
int. Works with LangChain too. Two things to remember: prefix search querie=
s with "Represent this sentence for searching relevant passages:", and chun=
k your text before 512 tokens or it gets cut off.
