<div style=3D"margin-top:0;">
<p style=3D"margin:0 0 15px 0;">You know how AI apps need to understand tex=
t meaning, not just keywords? That's what an <b>embedding model</b> does: i=
t converts text into numbers your app can compare. BGE Base is one of the b=
est English embedding models out there, and now it runs fully local, no Pyt=
hon, no PyTorch.</p><p style=3D"margin:0 0 15px 0;">Compendium Labs package=
d it into <b>GGUF format</b>, the same format you use for local LLMs, so on=
e runtime handles both your generator and your embedder. It hit 800,000 dow=
nloads.</p><p style=3D"margin:0 0 15px 0;">Pick your size:</p><ul><li><b>Q4=
_K_M at 66 MB</b>: small enough to bundle inside a desktop app</li><li>Q8_0=
 at 113 MB: better accuracy, still CPU-friendly</li><li>F16 at 209 MB: near=
-perfect precision for servers</li></ul><p style=3D"margin:0;">Spin it up w=
ith llama.cpp or Ollama and hit a local OpenAI-compatible endpoint. Works w=
ith LangChain too. Two things to remember: prefix search queries with "Repr=
esent this sentence for searching relevant passages:", and chunk your text =
before 512 tokens or it gets cut off.</p>
</div>
